 >       \@noitemerr
 >    \fi
 > }

what precisely does this gain you? if used with positive skips nothing =
as it
is identical to \addvspace and this is what \addvspace is used for (or =
should
be used for, the strange usage in list is something i wouldn't count =
here)

the logic is still as strange as before in the case \lastskip is =
negative and
skip positive.

 > It is quite possible that the special code for \lastskip=3D\z@ should =
